Subject: [PATCH] drm: let SET_MASTER take master over from another opener

docs/phase-3.md (ninth to tenth Ctrl+U) records this kernel change, but
the patch itself was never added to the repository. Without it
drm_hwcomposer, which runs as system without CAP_SYS_ADMIN, cannot
become DRM master once the minigbm allocator has opened /dev/dri/card0
first. It logs "DRM/KMS master access required", SurfaceFlinger never
gets a display, and the panel stays dark.

SET_MASTER is no longer gated on CAP_SYS_ADMIN, and it takes master over
from the current holder instead of returning -EBUSY. Access to the node
is still limited by its mode (0660 system graphics) and SELinux.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_auth.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_auth.c
@@ -249,15 +249,25 @@
 
 	guard(mutex)(&dev->master_mutex);
 
-	ret = drm_master_check_perm(dev, file_priv);
-	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+	/*
+	 * Kukui: drm_hwcomposer runs as system without CAP_SYS_ADMIN, and
+	 * the minigbm allocator opens the same primary node. Whichever opens
+	 * it first becomes master, so the composer could end up without it
+	 * and only ever create a null display. Access to the node is already
+	 * limited by its mode and SELinux, so SET_MASTER is not gated on
+	 * CAP_SYS_ADMIN, and a caller takes master over from the current
+	 * holder instead of getting -EBUSY.
+	 */
+	ret = 0;
 
 	if (drm_is_current_master_locked(file_priv))
 		return ret;
 
-	if (dev->master)
-		return -EBUSY;
+	if (dev->master) {
+		drm_info(dev, "SET_MASTER taken over by %s[%d]\n",
+			 current->comm, task_tgid_nr(current));
+		drm_master_put(&dev->master);
+	}
 
 	if (!file_priv->master)
 		return -EINVAL;
